abstract: >-
  PureByte is an architecture and an open runtime for AI Specialists: tiny
  models that read raw bytes and answer with decisions, scores and byte spans instead of
  generated text. A model combines a byte embedding, an optional hashed n-gram memory,
  ternary state-space blocks and task heads; the open runtime runs any model declared by a
  single GGUF file on ordinary CPUs, offline, with bit-identical results across kernels
  and thread counts on a platform. The training stack that builds, evaluates and exports new specialists
  from pinned public data is a separate repository,
  https://github.com/purebyte-ai/purebyte-train. Three example specialists detect
  credentials in source code and in binary files, and mask personal data.
keywords:
  - byte-level models
  - state-space models
  - ternary weights
  - small models
  - CPU inference
  - reproducible inference
  - secret detection
  - PII redaction
